# EAS archives from the git repo root, so this file lives here rather than in
# mobile/. Without it the tarball is 198 MB — ~125 MB of that is large tracked
# files under server/ (a Go installer .pkg and two compiled binaries) — and the
# upload dies with EPIPE partway through.
#
# The iOS build only needs mobile/, which has its own package.json and app.json
# and never reads a sibling directory. This affects the build archive only and
# changes nothing about what git tracks.
# NOT design-tokens: mobile/tailwind.config.js does
# require("../design-tokens/colors"), and NativeWind loads that config during
# the Bundle JavaScript phase. Excluding it failed the build there and nowhere
# earlier, which reads as a generic bundler error. It is 738 bytes — keep it.
/server
/app
/supabase
/skills
/.agents

# Generated locally; regenerated by prebuild or unused by the build.
mobile/ios
mobile/android
mobile/dist
mobile/.expo

# .git is 107 MB on its own — the same server/ binaries are in the history, and
# history is not reachable from a .easignore. The builder only needs a working
# tree, so excluding it takes the archive from 100 MB to ~2 MB.
.git

# This file REPLACES .gitignore for the build archive rather than adding to it
# (docs.expo.dev/build-reference/easignore), so anything .gitignore protects has
# to be repeated here or it ships to the builder. .env is the one that bites:
# EAS Build inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* from an uploaded .env into the bundle, so a
# local-only flag — EXPO_PUBLIC_QA_FORCE_TRACTION, say — would ride into a
# release build and stay true forever. Nothing is lost by excluding it: the
# preview profile takes its environment from EAS ("environment": "preview" in
# eas.json), which already carries all four EXPO_PUBLIC_* values the app needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
